  "_about": "a hen harrier quartering low over the moor: a slim, long-winged, long-tailed hawk, the wings held up in a shallow V -- the grey male: pale ash-grey above and on the hood, the belly and wing linings white, the outer primaries black as if dipped in ink, the white rump; the owl-like ruff round the face, the yellow eye, the small hooked black bill on its yellow cere; long thin yellow legs. Coats: ringtail (the brown female with the banded tail), marsh harrier. (rework/bigbirds/bigbirds.py)",
